   "subject": "Re: TechRepMixture & Fraction in the annotation file",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hi </span>Matthias,</font><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">The meaning of Mixture, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">TechRepMixture and </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Fraction are as follows:</span></font></div><div><ul><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Mixture: Mixture of samples labeled with different TMT reagents, which can be analyzed in\r\na single mass spectrometry experiment. </font></span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">TechRepMixture: Technical replicate ID of one mixture. One mixture may have multiple technical replicates. For example, if there are</font></span> two technical replicates of one mixture (such as Mixture1), then TechRepMixture = &quot;<i>1&quot; or &quot;2&quot;</i> and Mixture = &quot;<i>Mixture1</i>&quot;. </li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Fraction: Fraction ID. One technical replicate of one mixture may be fractionated into multiple fractions to increase the analytical depth. Then one technical replicate of one mixture\r\nshould correspond to multiple fractions. For example, if the first technical replicate of one mixture (such as Mixture1) has three fractions, then Fraction = &quot;<i>1&quot; or &quot;2&quot; or &quot;3&quot;</i>,  TechRepMixture= &quot;<i>1</i>&quot;,  Mixture = &quot;<i style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Mixture1</i><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">&quot;</span>.</font></span></li><li><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">BioReplicate : Unique ID for biological subject. If the channel doesn’t have sample, please\r\nadd ’Empty’ under BioReplicate.</font></li></ul><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Best,</font></div></div></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Ting</font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
